    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes. The combined milk fills $\\frac{19}{24}$ of one bottle.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{5}{12}&=\\frac{9}{24}+\\frac{10}{24}\\\\&=\\frac{19}{24}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\frac{19}{24}<1$, the milk can fit into a single bottle without overflowing.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
